  "evaluation": "C is best: it identifies both the inconsistency in Study A’s harm label and the distinction between a 15D depression dimension and a full depression scale, supporting apparent disagreement with reason outcome_measure. B reaches the same well-supported classification and captures the scale-direction issue, but C ties its explanation slightly more directly to the supplied fields. A recognizes the mislabeled improvement but incorrectly chooses design_or_bias: an uncontrolled design alone does not dissolve disagreement under the rules, and neither study is described as an underpowered null.",
